From: mqvpn contributors <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Schedule stream packets across active multipath paths

WLB reserves flow hash zero for packets that must use the MinRTT fallback,
but xquic assigns that value to every STREAM packet. That pins a single
TCP-lane stream to the lowest-SRTT path and prevents aggregation. STREAM
frames already carry offsets and are reordered by QUIC at the receiver, so
they can use WLB's unpinned per-packet WRR selection just like datagrams.

diff --git a/src/transport/xqc_packet_out.c b/src/transport/xqc_packet_out.c
--- a/src/transport/xqc_packet_out.c
+++ b/src/transport/xqc_packet_out.c
@@ -1247,6 +1247,14 @@ xqc_write_stream_frame_to_packet(xqc_connection_t *conn,
     stream->stream_conn->conn_flow_ctl.fc_data_sent += *send_data_written;
     packet_out->po_used_size += n_written;
     packet_out->po_stream_id = stream->stream_id;
     packet_out->po_stream_offset = stream->stream_send_offset;
+    /*
+     * WLB uses zero for packets that must take the MinRTT fallback. STREAM
+     * frames are independently ordered by QUIC using their offsets, so a
+     * stream packet can be scheduled by per-packet WRR and contribute to
+     * multipath aggregation. Keep the reserved unpinned sentinel distinct
+     * from both zero and a pinned flow hash.
+     */
+    packet_out->po_flow_hash = UINT32_MAX;
 
 #ifdef XQC_ENABLE_FEC
-- 
